Z||000008||Songman||06-14-2001||12:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87 Pegasus:<BR><B>why don't you try the texture spray paint they sell at home improvment stores...  i saw a blue with white specks in it... it looked pretty cool.  i picked up the black granit spray that turned out really good after you put that on you have to clear coat it to give it the shine and it is easier to clean </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Someone tried to texture paint the door trim in my T-top.. it looks hideous! I'd hold out for the carbon fiber... I have done a few things at my house with that texture paint. It is not as easy to make look good as you would think it is...<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
